WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.634 --> 00:00:03.903
-Welcome back to "Late Night."
We're here with Drew Barrymore.

00:00:03.903 --> 00:00:05.238
Now, I also --
Before we move on,

00:00:05.238 --> 00:00:06.372
I want to say congratulations.

00:00:06.372 --> 00:00:08.207
Six Daytime Emmy nominations.

00:00:08.207 --> 00:00:09.209
-Thank you.
-That's fantastic.

00:00:09.209 --> 00:00:11.544
Well-deserved for your show.

00:00:11.544 --> 00:00:14.279
Yeah, enjoy it!

00:00:14.279 --> 00:00:16.182
-I feel like relief is

00:00:16.182 --> 00:00:18.718
a huge definition of joy
right now, too.

00:00:18.718 --> 00:00:20.219
Like, just to be relieved.

00:00:20.219 --> 00:00:23.923
Like, I'm so relieved that it's
working, that we get to stay.

00:00:23.923 --> 00:00:25.191
-You get to keep doing
the show a third season.

00:00:25.191 --> 00:00:27.727
-I'm way too attached to it.

00:00:27.727 --> 00:00:30.296
All of my worth and happiness
is in this show.

00:00:30.296 --> 00:00:31.864
-Yeah.
They say that's very healthy.

00:00:31.864 --> 00:00:35.101
They say,
"Tie yourself to your work.

00:00:35.101 --> 00:00:36.603
Let that be
the only thing that brings you

00:00:36.603 --> 00:00:37.971
happiness and esteem," yeah.

00:00:37.971 --> 00:00:41.908
-It's so true.
I'm, like, way too invested.

00:00:41.908 --> 00:00:44.177
And, you know, season to season,
you don't know,

00:00:44.177 --> 00:00:46.212
and so you're kind of
going to that finish line

00:00:46.212 --> 00:00:48.347
and you just are --
Like, you see precipice

00:00:48.347 --> 00:00:50.850
and you get more and more
increasingly depressed

00:00:50.850 --> 00:00:53.886
at the idea of it
not coming back.

00:00:53.886 --> 00:00:56.589
And, you know, everyone's like,
"How are you in your life?"

00:00:56.589 --> 00:00:59.959
I wish I could just tell you I'm
so miserable, distracted,

00:00:59.959 --> 00:01:02.094
and screwed up,

00:01:02.094 --> 00:01:05.165
because I just really want
this to continue.

00:01:05.165 --> 00:01:06.699
Like, we're building
something here.

00:01:06.699 --> 00:01:08.067
-And it is. It gets better.
It's fantastic.

00:01:08.067 --> 00:01:09.635
-So I'm so relieved.

00:01:09.635 --> 00:01:11.137
-Well, we're very happy to share
your relief with you.

00:01:11.137 --> 00:01:12.338
-Thank you.

00:01:12.338 --> 00:01:14.240
-And it's coming across
as palpable relief.

00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:15.508
I will tell you that, as well.

00:01:15.508 --> 00:01:17.644
Hey, but you also find time
to -- Is this --

00:01:17.644 --> 00:01:18.811
You went crabbing.

00:01:18.811 --> 00:01:20.246
-I -- Well...

00:01:20.246 --> 00:01:22.115
-I feel like I've gone clamming,
but I've never gone crabbing.

00:01:22.115 --> 00:01:25.051
-And I want to clam.
-Yeah. [ Gasps ]

00:01:26.219 --> 00:01:29.421
Alright, so -- But this seems
like a lot more gear involved

00:01:29.421 --> 00:01:31.123
in crabbing,
'cause clamming is just like

00:01:31.123 --> 00:01:32.725
a rake and a bucket.

00:01:32.725 --> 00:01:35.862
-I really was
trying to be Nancy Meyers.

00:01:35.862 --> 00:01:38.664
Like, I wanted to picture myself
in a Nancy Meyers movie.

00:01:38.664 --> 00:01:41.734
I had three girls with me
and two dogs, no leashes.

00:01:41.734 --> 00:01:44.704
This is how it ended up.
That's the chicken.

00:01:44.704 --> 00:01:46.139
That's the bait.

00:01:46.139 --> 00:01:49.075
Just a nice, raw piece of
salmonella chicken hanging out.

00:01:49.075 --> 00:01:50.910
That's the back of my minivan.
-Great.

00:01:50.910 --> 00:01:54.948
-And Olive went, at one point --
'cause she's a very, like,

00:01:54.948 --> 00:01:57.116
rough-and-tumble,
like, cool girl,

00:01:57.116 --> 00:01:59.352
and she just threw the whole
bucket in at one point.

00:01:59.352 --> 00:02:01.887
And I was like,
"Olive! That doesn't have holes.

00:02:01.887 --> 00:02:04.490
It's gonna --" And there it was
just then floating down

00:02:04.490 --> 00:02:05.591
the river, and I was like,

00:02:05.591 --> 00:02:07.327
"We just littered, Olive!

00:02:07.327 --> 00:02:08.628
God, no!"

00:02:08.628 --> 00:02:11.097
And then this
kayaker woman came by,

00:02:11.097 --> 00:02:13.165
and she started screaming at me.

00:02:13.165 --> 00:02:15.401
And then I was like, of course,
I wanted to just, like,

00:02:15.401 --> 00:02:18.237
light into her, but I had
the three girls with me,

00:02:18.237 --> 00:02:20.206
so I was like,
"I can't do that."

00:02:20.206 --> 00:02:22.141
-Did she know who you were?

00:02:22.141 --> 00:02:23.476
-I don't care.
-Yeah.

00:02:23.476 --> 00:02:26.846
She was just --
She was out for blood.

00:02:26.846 --> 00:02:28.781
Like, she woke up
on the wrong side of the bed

00:02:28.781 --> 00:02:31.484
and was like, "Ooh,
I'm gonna take it out on you."

00:02:31.484 --> 00:02:35.054
And I was like, "And I'm gonna
keep it together."

00:02:35.054 --> 00:02:37.290
And she was like,
"It says, 'No parking'!

00:02:37.290 --> 00:02:38.757
I couldn't get my board in!"

00:02:38.757 --> 00:02:41.361
And I was like, "I am so sorry.
I did not see the sign."

00:02:41.361 --> 00:02:43.696
And literally two minutes later,
she's still lighting into me.

00:02:43.696 --> 00:02:45.931
And I'm like,
"No, I heard you,

00:02:45.931 --> 00:02:48.867
and I'm gonna get right on
moving that car right now.

00:02:48.867 --> 00:02:50.536
Little stuck, but right on it."

00:02:50.536 --> 00:02:54.907
And then, another minute later,
I'm like, "I'm on it!"

00:02:54.907 --> 00:02:58.144
And, you know, I just realized,
I'm not Nancy Meyers.

00:02:58.144 --> 00:02:59.512
I'm "Jackass."
-Yeah.

00:02:59.512 --> 00:03:00.846
Have you ever --

00:03:00.846 --> 00:03:03.049
-I've got the thing, and I'm so
worried about her seeing

00:03:03.049 --> 00:03:05.084
the bucket go down the river.

00:03:05.084 --> 00:03:06.452
Oh, that would have given
her more ammunition.

00:03:06.452 --> 00:03:08.320
-All of a sudden, she's kayaking
back, making another loop.

00:03:08.320 --> 00:03:11.224
-Oh, she'd have called the
authorities, I'm telling you.

00:03:11.224 --> 00:03:12.858
-Has anybody ever been
yelling at you,

00:03:12.858 --> 00:03:15.128
and then they recognize
you mid-yell?

00:03:15.128 --> 00:03:16.729
I've had that happen,
which is pretty fun.

00:03:16.729 --> 00:03:18.063
-Oh, what was that like?

00:03:18.063 --> 00:03:21.500
-I was running, and a car
was coming out of a driveway.

00:03:21.500 --> 00:03:24.169
And they looked one way,
but not the other,

00:03:24.169 --> 00:03:26.872
and so they cut right into me,
like, where I was running.

00:03:26.872 --> 00:03:28.808
And so I had to dodge the car.

00:03:28.808 --> 00:03:31.277
And I'm not proud of this, okay?
I'm not a hero in this story.

00:03:31.277 --> 00:03:33.078
-I was gonna say,
"What did you do in this?"

00:03:33.078 --> 00:03:34.914
-And so I, like,
slapped the hood of the car

00:03:34.914 --> 00:03:36.248
and was like,
"Watch where you're going!"

00:03:36.248 --> 00:03:38.084
And the guy was like,
"You watch where -- Hey!"

00:03:38.084 --> 00:03:40.987
-Yeah!
[ Laughs ]

00:03:40.987 --> 00:03:43.822
Well, I'm glad to know
that you react.

00:03:43.822 --> 00:03:46.659
If those kids weren't around,
I would have taken out

00:03:46.659 --> 00:03:48.461
all my anger right back out
on this woman,

00:03:48.461 --> 00:03:49.761
'cause she was ready to go.

00:03:49.761 --> 00:03:51.130
She had the gloves on.

00:03:51.130 --> 00:03:53.532
She had the attitude.
She was like a dog with a bone.

00:03:53.532 --> 00:03:54.767
She wouldn't let it go.

00:03:54.767 --> 00:03:57.036
-By the way, she should also be,
you know,

00:03:57.036 --> 00:03:58.504
cognizant of the fact
that kids are around.

00:03:58.504 --> 00:04:00.672
It's amazing when people
still want to have a thing

00:04:00.672 --> 00:04:01.674
where you're like,
"Okay, I get it.

00:04:01.674 --> 00:04:03.109
I did the wrong thing."

00:04:03.109 --> 00:04:06.478
-I did. I was like, "I got it.
I got the kids. I got the dogs."

00:04:06.478 --> 00:04:07.746
-You should have blamed it
on the kids and be like,

00:04:07.746 --> 00:04:10.717
"They're the ones
who parked the car."

00:04:10.717 --> 00:04:13.586
-"Would you like
a piece of raw chicken?

00:04:13.586 --> 00:04:15.087
Maybe you can catch a crab."

00:04:15.087 --> 00:04:16.555
-Well, you sent us this picture,
as well.

00:04:16.555 --> 00:04:18.123
-That's Lucy, my dog.

00:04:18.123 --> 00:04:19.792
-Great. And is she, like,

00:04:19.792 --> 00:04:21.494
on the lookout for crabs
in this picture?

00:04:21.494 --> 00:04:23.262
-She's on the lookout to
make this

00:04:23.262 --> 00:04:24.430
as hair ball as possible,

00:04:24.430 --> 00:04:27.166
because, of course,
I'm not there kind of

00:04:27.166 --> 00:04:28.434
controlling the situation.

00:04:28.434 --> 00:04:30.637
Like, I think
I actually really --

00:04:30.637 --> 00:04:33.005
The truth is, I just --
I am chaos.

00:04:33.005 --> 00:04:35.675
Like, I want it to be
cute and pretty, but it isn't.

00:04:35.675 --> 00:04:36.809
It's messy.

00:04:36.809 --> 00:04:38.711
And the kids are
running around and the crabs

00:04:38.711 --> 00:04:39.812
and the raw chicken
and the dog --

00:04:39.812 --> 00:04:40.980
-Did you catch any crab?

00:04:40.980 --> 00:04:42.514
-Not a one.
-Yeah.

00:04:42.514 --> 00:04:43.783
Because let me
tell you something.

00:04:43.783 --> 00:04:45.851
You know why I thought you might
not have caught any?

00:04:45.851 --> 00:04:48.187
Because here are the
three pictures you sent.

00:04:48.521 --> 00:04:53.125
Like, this is like, "Hey,
how was your crabbing trip?"

00:04:53.125 --> 00:04:56.362
"Well, we had this
and this and a dog."

00:04:56.362 --> 00:04:57.696
You'd be like...

00:04:57.696 --> 00:05:00.266
-So, we get in the car,
and the kids all look at me,

00:05:00.266 --> 00:05:01.834
the three girls, and I'm like,

00:05:01.834 --> 00:05:03.669
"Gosh, you guys,
that really sucked.

00:05:03.669 --> 00:05:06.072
We got in trouble. We littered.

00:05:06.072 --> 00:05:08.141
Like, we didn't catch a crab.

00:05:08.141 --> 00:05:10.075
I think we have salmonella."

00:05:10.075 --> 00:05:13.479
And my little one, Frankie, was
like, "I think we get a 'C.'"

00:05:13.479 --> 00:05:16.916
And then Olive's friend,
Olympia, was like, "A 'C.'"

00:05:16.916 --> 00:05:18.884
And I looked at Olive,
and she goes, "D-minus."

00:05:18.884 --> 00:05:20.953
And I was like,
"Thank you, Olive.

00:05:20.953 --> 00:05:23.022
One above failure. That's it?"

00:05:23.022 --> 00:05:25.290
-I really like that
Frankie gave it a "C."

00:05:25.290 --> 00:05:26.993
I feel like that's really kind.

00:05:26.993 --> 00:05:29.995
-She's much more optimistic.
Olive's more of a realist.

00:05:29.995 --> 00:05:32.799
-That's a very big heart
to give you a "C" on that.

00:05:32.799 --> 00:05:35.968
-Well, to come full circle,
I didn't grow up around kids,

00:05:35.968 --> 00:05:37.002
but my whole --

00:05:37.002 --> 00:05:38.270
-Or crabs, I'm guessing,

00:05:38.270 --> 00:05:39.705
based on how that went.

00:05:39.705 --> 00:05:42.374
-No, I know.
And I need a lesson in crabs.

00:05:42.374 --> 00:05:45.178
So if anybody has
some crab tips, I'm all ears.

00:05:45.178 --> 00:05:47.346
-And, again, don't take it
out of context.

00:05:47.346 --> 00:05:48.414
-Yeah, exactly.

00:05:48.414 --> 00:05:50.216
-I noticed a few
scattered laughs there.

00:05:50.216 --> 00:05:52.618
We've established what crabs
we're talking about!

00:05:52.618 --> 00:05:54.954
-Edible ones!
-The ones in this picture.

00:05:54.954 --> 00:05:56.922
Oh, wait. Oh, wait.

00:05:56.922 --> 00:05:59.659
No, there's no
actual photos of crabs.

00:05:59.659 --> 00:06:04.063
-But now, literally,
my days are spent with kids,

00:06:04.063 --> 00:06:05.664
hanging out with them,
having the best time ever,

00:06:05.664 --> 00:06:06.899
failing at crabbing.

00:06:06.899 --> 00:06:08.434
-That is really funny
that you were a kid who

00:06:08.434 --> 00:06:09.702
hung out with adults

00:06:09.702 --> 00:06:11.537
and now you're an adult who
hangs out with kids.

00:06:11.537 --> 00:06:14.139
-Almost exclusively.

00:06:14.139 --> 00:06:16.676
My whole life has
actually flipped on its head.

00:06:16.676 --> 00:06:20.312
And I am happy living in
New York.

00:06:20.312 --> 00:06:21.914
I was a kid who grew up in L.A.

00:06:21.914 --> 00:06:23.149
So, yeah, I'm kind of on
the "B" side of the record.

00:06:23.149 --> 00:06:24.584
-Has it been nice?

00:06:24.584 --> 00:06:28.020
And do the families -- Did you
say "'B' side of the record"

00:06:28.020 --> 00:06:29.455
and then gesture
towards the band?

00:06:29.455 --> 00:06:30.890
-Yes, I did.

00:06:30.890 --> 00:06:35.527
-That is as depressing as making
multiple jokes for stepfathers

00:06:35.527 --> 00:06:37.630
and then begging them
to respond.

00:06:37.630 --> 00:06:40.199
-You know those
old, delicious 45s.

00:06:40.199 --> 00:06:41.367
I'm on the "B" side.

00:06:41.367 --> 00:06:42.401
-And you're happy to be back
in New York City?

00:06:42.401 --> 00:06:43.702
We're certainly happy
to have you.

00:06:43.702 --> 00:06:48.140
-I love that my life and the
chapters took me here.

00:06:48.140 --> 00:06:50.175
Someone said like, "Oh, this
could be your forever home."

00:06:50.175 --> 00:06:52.645
And I was like, "I don't know
what my life will ever be.

00:06:52.645 --> 00:06:55.547
We will always be
on a learned journey."

00:06:55.547 --> 00:06:57.182
And then, every once in a while,
you can stop

00:06:57.182 --> 00:06:58.951
and be like, "Whoa!

00:06:58.951 --> 00:07:00.853
Cool. This is where I'm at now."

00:07:00.853 --> 00:07:02.654
-Well, we're so happy
you're here.

00:07:02.654 --> 00:07:04.157
We're so happy
you're here tonight.

00:07:04.157 --> 00:07:05.491
We're so happy
you're feeling better.

00:07:05.491 --> 00:07:06.558
And thank you so much --

00:07:06.558 --> 00:07:08.794
-That voicemail.
-That voicemail.

00:07:08.794 --> 00:07:11.196
May you all be so lucky to
receive a voicemail like that.

00:07:11.196 --> 00:07:12.331
Drew Barrymore, everybody.

00:07:12.331 --> 00:07:14.500
-I love you.
-I love you, too.

00:07:14.500 --> 00:07:16.468
"Drew Barrymore Show"
airs weekdays,

00:07:16.468 --> 00:07:17.703
so check your local listings.

00:07:17.703 --> 00:07:19.472
We'll be right back with
Chris Parnell.

00:07:19.472 --> 00:07:21.474
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

